---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { githubStarsLabel } from "../github";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL, UPSTREAM_URL } from "../site";

const starsLabel = await githubStarsLabel();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms · Matebot"
  description="The licence and terms for using Matebot."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header starsLabel={starsLabel} />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p><strong>Last updated: November 5, 2026</strong></p>
      <p>
        Matebot is open source software you can run yourself, and it can also be offered to you as a
        service by whoever operates the Matebot you sign in to. The{" "}
        <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Apache License 2.0</a> in this repository governs your
        use of the code. The operator of the server you connect to is responsible for that deployment,
        including any paid plan it offers and its own terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Open-source software</h2>
      <p>
        The Matebot source code is available under the{" "}
        <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Apache License 2.0</a>. That license, not this page,
        governs your use of the code. Matebot is a fork of the Apache-2.0{" "}
        <a href={UPSTREAM_URL}>Rakazo</a> project by Inbox Zero Inc., and the upstream copyright notices
        and license text carry over unchanged. The upstream project is credited; the Matebot name and the
        changes in this repository are not the upstream project's.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        Accounts are created on the server you connect to, and that server's operator decides who may sign
        up. You must be at least 13 years old, and old enough to form a binding contract where you live, to
        use the software. Keep your sign-in details and connected credentials secure. You are responsible
        for activity in your account.
      </p>

      <h2>Bots and AI output</h2>
      <p>
        Bots act with the instructions, permissions, and connected accounts you give them, including
        when you are not watching, such as in scheduled routines. Actions your bots take, such as
        sending messages, changing data, making purchases, or running commands, are taken on your
        behalf and are your responsibility. Give bots only the access they need, and require approval
        for actions that are hard to undo.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI output can be inaccurate or incomplete. Review it before you rely on it. Do not use
        Matebot where an error could cause death, injury, or serious harm, or to make decisions with legal,
        medical, or financial consequences for others without qualified human review.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not use Matebot to break the law, to attack or overload systems you do not own, to send spam, or
        to violate the terms of the model, computer, or integration providers you connect. Operators may
        limit or stop access to their deployment for misuse.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The software is provided "as is", without warranties or conditions of any kind, as set out in the
        Apache License 2.0. To the extent permitted by law, the authors and contributors are not liable for
        any loss arising from your use of the software.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        This repository's terms page may change as the project does. Changes to the software itself are
        recorded in the <a href={GITHUB_URL}>repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Paid plans</h2>
      <p>
        Some deployments offer paid features. Any such plan, its price, what it includes, how it renews,
        how it can be cancelled, and how a refund is handled are set by the operator of the server you
        signed in to, and are shown to you before you pay. Payment is taken by that operator's payment
        processor. This page does not set those terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you cancel, access to paid features ends as described by that operator. Deleting your account
        removes your data from that deployment as described in the{" "}
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Open an issue in the <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}>Matebot repository</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
